---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../../components/Diagram.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import { page } from "../../lib/nav.ts";

const S = "server/src/iki_server/entities/services.py";
const ST = "server/src/iki_server/entities/states.py";
const at = (label: string) => page(label).href;

const life = [
  { id: "manifest", x: 20, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Type manifest", sub: "a plugin's types/*.yaml", href: at("Types and tables") },
  { id: "tables", x: 200, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Typed tables", sub: "row, __history, lists", href: at("Types and tables") },
  { id: "create", x: 380, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Create", sub: "prepare, then write", strong: true, href: at("Saving and validation") },
  { id: "revisions", x: 560, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Revisions", sub: "append-only; the ETag", href: at("Revisions and history") },
  { id: "state", x: 740, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Set a state", sub: "set_by, holds, guards", href: at("States and guards") },
  { id: "refs", x: 20, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "References", sub: "foreign keys; graph edges", href: at("Links between records") },
  { id: "entry", x: 200, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Registry entry", sub: "found by identity", href: at("Identity and HRIDs") },
  { id: "rules", x: 380, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Rules", sub: "CEL at every save", href: at("Saving and validation") },
  { id: "locked", x: 560, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Locked", sub: "a database trigger", href: at("Locks and corrections") },
  { id: "signatures", x: 740, y: 170, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Signatures", sub: "sign in again; Ed25519", href: at("Electronic signatures") },
  { id: "correction", x: 380, y: 300, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Correction", sub: "a return, with a reason", href: at("Locks and corrections") },
  { id: "audit", x: 740, y: 300, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Audit log", sub: "append-only events", href: at("Audit trail") },
];
const lifeEdges = [
  { from: "manifest", to: "tables" },
  { from: "tables", to: "create" },
  { from: "create", to: "revisions" },
  { from: "revisions", to: "state" },
  { from: "tables", to: "refs", label: "ref fields", dashed: true },
  { from: "create", to: "entry", label: "identity", dashed: true },
  { from: "create", to: "rules", label: "every save", dashed: true },
  { from: "state", to: "signatures", label: "if signed" },
  { from: "state", to: "locked", label: "locks: true" },
  { from: "signatures", to: "locked", label: "the last one" },
  { from: "locked", to: "correction", label: "an edit, or a reversal" },
  { from: "correction", to: "revisions", label: "back to review", via: [[545, 330], [545, 85]] as [number, number][], at: [545, 280] as [number, number] },
  { from: "signatures", to: "audit", label: "signature.signed" },
];
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: "What a record is" },
  { id: "how", label: "From a type manifest to a signed, locked record" },
  { id: "pages", label: "Which page covers what" },
  { id: "ref", label: "Where the code is" },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title="What a record is">
    <p>
      A record is a row of a type that a plugin declared. Every change to it is a numbered,
      append-only revision, and the revision number is what a client must name to change it again.
      A type may give it state fields. Setting a state is checked by the plugin's roles and guards,
      may need electronic signatures bound to that exact revision, and may lock the record so that
      the database itself refuses to change it. A locked record changes again only after a state
      that doesn't lock is set: by a reasoned correction, or by a signed reversal when the lock was
      signed for. Records live in projects; what a thing <em>is</em> (its identity) lives once, in
      the registry, as an entry every project's record points to.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>One table per type, with a history table beside it (<Adr n={[7, 33]} />).</li>
      <li>Provenance is the revision that last changed a field; there's no separate table (<Adr n="0035" />).</li>
      <li>States, locks, guards and signatures are the plugin's to declare (<Adr n={[125, 128, 126]} />).</li>
      <li>Registries keep identities; each project keeps its own record (<Adr n="0115" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title="From a type manifest to a signed, locked record">
    <p>
      A plugin's type manifest is compiled into a Django model and its tables. Creating a record
      checks every value and the plugin's rules, then writes the row, revision 1 and its history in
      one transaction. Each edit is another revision. A state field is never set by an edit: it's
      set on its own, by someone with a role its state allows, once its holds and guards pass and
      any signatures it needs are given. A locking state makes the database refuse every change to
      the record's tables until a state that doesn't lock is set. Each box below opens the page
      that covers it.
    </p>
    <Diagram
      id="life"
      title="A record's life, from its type to its audit trail"
      width={910}
      height={380}
      boxes={life}
      edges={lifeEdges}
      caption="Solid arrows are the order things happen in; dashed ones are what every save keeps or checks."
    >
      <div slot="manifest">
        <p>An <code>EntityType</code> under a plugin's <code>types/</code>: fields, an optional <code>identity</code>, state fields, rules and display (<Adr n={[32, 38]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/core/types" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="tables">
        <p>The type's table extends <code>Entity</code>; beside it a <code>__history</code> table, a table per list of references, files, people or rows, and <code>__entry</code> tables for an identity (<Adr n="0033" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="codegen/src/iki_codegen/models.py" sym="def render_models(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="create">
        <p><code>POST /api/v1/entities</code>: everything is checked first, then written in one transaction.</p>
        <p><Path p={S} sym="def create(" />, <Path p={S} sym="def prepare(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="revisions">
        <p>Each change writes a <code>Revision</code> and a history row per table it touched. <code>Entity.revision</code> is the API's ETag (<Adr n="0035" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={S} sym="def _revise(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="state">
        <p><code>POST /api/v1/entities/{"{ref}"}/states/{"{field}"}</code>, under the row lock: roles (<code>set_by</code>), holds, guards, then the reason (<Adr n={[125, 128]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={ST} sym="def set_state(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="refs">
        <p>A <code>ref</code> field is a foreign key; a list of them is a table. Triggers keep an edge per reference in the graph that lineage walks (<Adr n="0123" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/graph/edges.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="entry">
        <p>A type with an <code>identity</code> is registered: the create finds or makes the registry's entry, and the project's record points to it (<Adr n="0115" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={S} sym="def _find_entry(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="rules">
        <p>Plugins' <code>check</code> rules are CEL, run by iki-wasm on every save; <code>unique</code> and <code>no_overlap</code> are held by triggers. A rule can hold a record for review (<Adr n="0127" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/entities/checking.py" sym="def broken(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="locked">
        <p>A locking state puts its field in <code>Entity.locked_by</code>; a trigger on the type's tables refuses any write while it's not empty (<Adr n="0120" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={ST} sym="def install_guards(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="signatures">
        <p>Each signer signs in again; Iki signs a canonical document naming the record's content hash at that revision with the deployment's Ed25519 key. The last signature sets the state (<Adr n={[124, 126]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/signatures/services.py" sym="def _sign(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="correction">
        <p>An unsigned lock can name an <code>on_edit</code> state: the edit returns to it and changes the values in one transaction. A signed lock is reopened by a signed reversal (<Adr n={[179, 126]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={ST} sym="def return_for_edit(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="audit">
        <p>Events are written in the change's transaction and can't be changed. State changes, holds, links and signatures are audited; a plain edit's revision is its trail (<Adr n="0025" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/audit/log.py" sym="ACTIONS" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>

    <h3 id="pages">Which page covers what</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><PageLink to="Types and tables" />: how a manifest becomes tables, and what the deploy adds to them.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Identity and HRIDs" />: registries, entries and project records, HRIDs, accessions and registrars.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Saving and validation" />: one create or edit, step by step; CEL rules, holds, unique and no-overlap.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Revisions and history" />: revisions, the ETag, history tables, provenance, archiving, and who and which agent made a change.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="States and guards" />: state fields, who sets each state, guards, and a plasmid verification's review as the worked example.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Locks and corrections" />: how the database holds a lock, corrections, and the reason every edit after an unlock needs.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Electronic signatures" />: Part 11 signing, what's signed, lapsed signatures and signed reversals.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Links between records" />: references and lists of them, how they're read, and the graph lineage walks.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Audit trail" />: the append-only audit log, and the database roles that keep it so.</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title="Where the code is">
    <ul>
      <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/entities" />: records, states, rules, holds and registries</li>
      <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/signatures" />: electronic signatures</li>
      <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/graph" />: the graph of references and lineage</li>
      <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/audit" />: the audit log and agents</li>
      <li><Path p="codegen/src/iki_codegen/models.py" />: a type's tables</li>
      <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/sync.py" />: the triggers a deploy installs</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
